# Diffo-Dev Engines

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:artefact_kino, "~> 0.1.4"},
  {:req, "~> 0.5"}
])
```

## Overview

This livebook should be read after Knowing the diffo-dev Lore livebook [![Run in Livebook](https://livebook.dev/badge/v1/blue.svg)](https://livebook.dev/run?url=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdiffo-dev%2F.github%2Fblob%2Fmain%2Flivebook%2Flore.livemd)

This livebook uses Artefact and ArtefactKino from [Artefactory](https://github.com/diffo-dev/artefactory). ArtefactKino is a viewer.

```elixir
require Artefact
defmodule Util do
  def relabel({node_ref, node}, labels) do
    {node_ref, Keyword.replace(node, :labels, labels)}
  end

  def load(nil, name) do
    binary = Req.get!("https://raw.githubusercontent.com/diffo-dev/.github/main/data/#{name}.bin", raw: true).body
    :erlang.binary_to_term(binary)
  end

  def load(path, name) do
    binary = File.read!("#{path}/#{name}.bin")
    :erlang.binary_to_term(binary)
  end
end


# path = "git/diffo-dev.github/data/" # local file base path
# path = nil # to load from repository
path = "git/diffo-dev.github/data"
```

## Engines

According to our lore we do Thinking with Minds of different kind. Minds may have Engines which have a native Artefact form.

### Engines Model

In the engine model:

* An engine is continuously engineered
* Each engine has a lifecycle
* An engine does work
* An engine consumes resources, and may produce them
* Some engines are better than others for different work
* The universe of engines is infinite
* An engine is an expression of ingenuity

In our case of engine/s implementing Mind, the work of the engine is to transform artefacts. We'll explore different minds, different engines and their native artefact forms.

## Artefact Representation (work in progress)

### My Mind Realized

My Mind is Realised by Engines.

```elixir
my_mind_artefact = Util.load(path, "my_mind")

engine = {:engine, [labels: ["Engine"], properties: %{"name" => "engine"}, uuid: "019e04de-8215-7b7c-acb6-8ef0af6f59a7"]}
mind_engine_relationship = [from: :mind, type: "OPERATES", to: :engine]
engine_artefact_relationship = [from: :engine, type: "PROCESSES", to: :artefact]

args = [
  nodes: [
    {:mind, [uuid: "019ddb71-ed63-73e3-adeb-328290e8294e"]},
    {:artefact, [uuid: "019e04dd-182f-7f28-acb8-8cbf06a6520d"]},
    engine,
  ],
  relationships: [
    mind_engine_relationship ,
    engine_artefact_relationship
  ]
]
   
my_mind_realized_artefact =
  my_mind_artefact
  |> Artefact.graft(args, title: "My Mind Realized",  description: "My Mind is Realised by Engines.")

ArtefactKino.new(my_mind_realized_artefact)
```

### My Kinship Mind Realized

My Kinship Mind is Realized Graphically

```elixir
my_kinship_mind_artefact = Util.load(path, "thinking/my_kinship_mind")

graph_engine = {:graph_engine, [labels: ["Engine"], properties: %{"name" => "graph_engine"}, 
      uuid: "019e04d6-23af-7c69-b8b0-6942b22a0af8"]}
graph_artefact = {:graph_artefact, [labels: ["Artefact"], properties: %{"name" => "graph_artefact"}, 
      uuid: "019e04e0-61f2-7b60-ab36-39325064facb"]}

args = [
  nodes: [
    {:artefact, [uuid: "019e04dd-182f-7f28-acb8-8cbf06a6520d"]},
    engine,
    graph_artefact,
    graph_engine
  ],
  relationships: [
    [from: :artefact, type: "REALIZED_BY", to: :graph_artefact],
    [from: :engine, type: "REALIZED_BY", to: :graph_engine],
    [from: :graph_engine, type: "FLUENT_IN", to: :graph_artefact],
  ]
  
]

my_kinship_mind_realized_artefact =
  my_mind_realized_artefact
  |> Artefact.combine(my_kinship_mind_artefact)
  |> Artefact.graft(args, title: "My Kinship Mind Realized", 
    description: "My Kinship Mind is Realized Graphically.")

ArtefactKino.new(my_kinship_mind_realized_artefact)
```

